entries.explanation_en:
An electrically neutral elementary particle with an extremely small rest mass, denoted by $
u$ (with its corresponding antiparticle being the antineutrino $	ilde{
u}$). In $ eta$ decay, a neutrino ($
u$) is emitted alongside a positron in $ eta^+$ decay, whereas an antineutrino ($	ilde{
u}$) is emitted alongside an electron in $ eta^-$ decay.

